# Environment for homelab-release-run.sh. Rendered at DEPLOY time, when the
# vault is available, and read at RUN time from this file — never looked up as
# a vault variable by the playbook itself. The weekly report executes from the
# runner's `git archive` checkout, in which the vault does not exist, so a
# vault_ reference there would be undefined exactly where it is needed. That
# mistake was made once already (b77f27f) by an assert that passed on the
# workstation and failed on all three hosts at 04:01.
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN is OPTIONAL and normally empty. Unauthenticated GitHub allows 60
# requests an hour per IP; a full run costs about 45, and the first live run on
# 2026-08-05 ran out on its 48th image and reported `error` for it — correctly,
# and visibly, but a report that is one flaky retry from incomplete is worth
# fixing rather than admiring. A token raises the limit to 5000/hour.
#
# It needs NO SCOPES. Every repository this reads is public; the token is here
# purely to raise the rate limit, so a classic token with nothing ticked, or a
# fine-grained token with "Public repositories (read-only)", is correct. Do not
# grant it more — this file is 0600 root-owned, but a token that can only count
# faster is a different blast radius from one that can write.
GITHUB_TOKEN={{ vault_github_token | default('') }}
